IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: ss 13 to 15 -- the Court's order to make good a default in filing a return, the relodging of a lost registered document,
-- and the Registrar's notice that a document delivered is not of the standard size, durability and legibility. Layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- s 15(1) (the Minister's power to prescribe the requirements by regulations) is machinery and is not coded (NOTES.md: inert, reason 2). ss 16 and 16A are shown repealed in the text.
-- The Court and the Registrar appear only as holders of powers and duties over the corporation or person; there is no seat for them.
--
-- The 14 days of s 13(1) are the text's own words and are counted only by sg-periods.l4 ("within 14 days after" reads the day of service as in time: fork line F-H-P2 in NOTES.md).
-- The 14 days of s 15(4) are a "14th day after": the last day is the date of service plus 14 days (convention P1).
-- No regulative rule is written for s 13(1): the 14 days are a condition of the Court's power, and the text states no duty with a deadline there (fork line F-H-D2 in NOTES.md).

§ `Section 13: enforcement of the duty to make returns`

-- The failure to make good the default within 14 days after service of the notice. No day on which it was made good means it has not been made good.
-- src:3379 | 13.—(1) If a corporation or person, having made default in
-- src:3380 | complying with —
-- src:3382 | (a) any provision of this Act or of any other law (other than the
-- src:3383 | Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018)
-- src:3384 | which requires the filing or lodging in any manner with
-- src:3385 | the Registrar of any return, account or other document or
-- src:3386 | the giving of notice to the Registrar of any matter;
-- src:3388 | (b) any request of the Registrar to amend or complete and
-- src:3389 | resubmit any document or to submit a fresh document; or
-- src:3391 | (c) any request of the Registrar under section 12D(7) to rectify
-- src:3392 | any error, defect or inaccuracy in any particulars or
-- src:3393 | document in the register,
-- src:3395 | fails to make good the default within 14 days after the service on the
-- src:3396 | corporation or person of a notice requiring it to be done, the Court
-- src:3397 | may, on an application by any member or creditor of the corporation
@ref s 13(1) (src:3379-3397)
GIVEN `the day the notice requiring the default to be made good was served on the corporation or person` IS A DATE
      `the day the default was made good, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(1) the corporation or person failed to make good the default within 14 days after the service of the notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the default was made good, if it was`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST madeGood THEN
        (NOT (`period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the notice requiring the default to be made good was served on the corporation or person` madeGood 14 Days))

-- (1): "If a corporation or person, having made default in complying with (a) ... (b) ... (c) ..., fails to make good the default within 14 days after the service ... of a notice requiring it to be done, the Court may, on an application by any member or creditor of the corporation or by the Registrar, make an order".
-- A grant gated by "If": NOTHING when the gate fails (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line F-H-S3). "(other than the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018)" closes paragraph (a) in the text's own words: JUST FALSE.
-- src:3379 | 13.—(1) If a corporation or person, having made default in
-- src:3380 | complying with —
-- src:3382 | (a) any provision of this Act or of any other law (other than the
-- src:3383 | Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018)
-- src:3384 | which requires the filing or lodging in any manner with
-- src:3385 | the Registrar of any return, account or other document or
-- src:3386 | the giving of notice to the Registrar of any matter;
-- src:3388 | (b) any request of the Registrar to amend or complete and
-- src:3389 | resubmit any document or to submit a fresh document; or
-- src:3391 | (c) any request of the Registrar under section 12D(7) to rectify
-- src:3392 | any error, defect or inaccuracy in any particulars or
-- src:3393 | document in the register,
-- src:3395 | fails to make good the default within 14 days after the service on the
-- src:3396 | corporation or person of a notice requiring it to be done, the Court
-- src:3397 | may, on an application by any member or creditor of the corporation
-- src:3402 | or by the Registrar, make an order directing the corporation and any
-- src:3403 | officer of the corporation or such person to make good the default
-- src:3404 | within such time as is specified in the order.
@ref s 13(1) (src:3379-3404)
GIVEN `the corporation or person made default in complying with a provision of this Act or of another law requiring the filing or lodging with the Registrar of a return, account or other document or the giving of notice to the Registrar of a matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is imposed by the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation or person made default in complying with a request of the Registrar to amend or complete and resubmit a document or to submit a fresh document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation or person made default in complying with a request of the Registrar under section 12D(7) to rectify an error, defect or inaccuracy in particulars or a document in the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation or person failed to make good the default within 14 days after the service of the notice requiring it to be done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a member or creditor of the corporation, or the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13(1) the Court may order the corporation and any officer of the corporation or such person to make good the default` MEANS
    IF    `the corporation or person made default in complying with a request of the Registrar to amend or complete and resubmit a document or to submit a fresh document`
       OR `the corporation or person made default in complying with a request of the Registrar under section 12D(7) to rectify an error, defect or inaccuracy in particulars or a document in the register`
       OR (`the corporation or person made default in complying with a provision of this Act or of another law requiring the filing or lodging with the Registrar of a return, account or other document or the giving of notice to the Registrar of a matter` AND (NOT `the requirement is imposed by the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`))
    THEN (IF `the corporation or person failed to make good the default within 14 days after the service of the notice requiring it to be done`
          THEN (IF `the applicant is a member or creditor of the corporation, or the Registrar`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the order is "on an application by any member or creditor of the corporation or by the Registrar"; the text says nothing of an application by anyone else (split site (ii), fork line F-H-S3)
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power arises "If" the corporation or person "fails to make good the default within 14 days after the service ... of a notice requiring it to be done"; the text says nothing of a default made good in time (grant ruling, limit 1; split site (ii), fork line F-H-S3)
    ELSE (IF `the corporation or person made default in complying with a provision of this Act or of another law requiring the filing or lodging with the Registrar of a return, account or other document or the giving of notice to the Registrar of a matter` AND `the requirement is imposed by the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any provision of this Act or of any other law (other than the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018) which requires the filing or lodging in any manner with the Registrar of any return, account or other document" (paragraph (a) excludes the Act named; a default under (b) or (c) is decided above)
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says nothing of a default of any other kind

DECLARE `s 13(2) bearer of the costs` IS ONE OF
    `s 13(2) the corporation`
    `s 13(2) an officer of the corporation`
    `s 13(2) such person`
    `s 13(2) someone else`

-- src:3410 | (2) Any such order may provide that all costs of and incidental to
-- src:3411 | the application must be borne by the corporation or by any officer of
-- src:3412 | the corporation responsible for the default or by such person.
@ref s 13(2) (src:3410-3412)
GIVEN `the order is an order under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      bearer IS A `s 13(2) bearer of the costs`
      `the officer is responsible for the default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13(2) the order may provide that all costs of and incidental to the application must be borne by the bearer` MEANS
    IF `the order is an order under subsection (1)`
    THEN (CONSIDER bearer
          WHEN `s 13(2) the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 13(2) such person` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 13(2) an officer of the corporation` THEN (IF `the officer is responsible for the default` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by any officer of the corporation responsible for the default"; the text says nothing of an officer who is not responsible
          OTHERWISE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the costs "must be borne by the corporation or by any officer of the corporation responsible for the default or by such person"; the text does not say "only"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any such order" is an order under subsection (1); the text says nothing of any other order

-- (3): "Nothing in this section limits the operation of any written law imposing penalties": a flat negative.
-- src:3414 | (3) Nothing in this section limits the operation of any written law
-- src:3415 | imposing penalties on a corporation or its officers or such person in
-- src:3416 | respect of any such default.
@ref s 13(3) (src:3414-3416)
GIVEN `the written law imposes penalties on a corporation or its officers or such person in respect of the default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13(3) this section limits the operation of the written law` MEANS
    IF `the written law imposes penalties on a corporation or its officers or such person in respect of the default`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section limits the operation of any written law imposing penalties on a corporation or its officers or such person in respect of any such default" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence speaks only of "any written law imposing penalties ... in respect of any such default"; the text says nothing of any other law

§ `Section 14: relodging of lost registered documents`

-- src:3420 | 14.—(1) If in the case of any corporation incorporated or registered
-- src:3421 | under this Act or any corresponding previous written law the
-- src:3422 | constitution or any other document relating to the corporation filed or
-- src:3423 | lodged with the Registrar has been lost or destroyed, the corporation
-- src:3424 | may apply to the Registrar for permission to lodge a copy of the
-- src:3425 | document as originally filed or lodged.
@ref s 14(1) (src:3420-3425)
GIVEN `the corporation was incorporated or registered under this Act or a corresponding previous written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution or another document relating to the corporation, filed or lodged with the Registrar, has been lost or destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(1) the corporation may apply to the Registrar for permission to lodge a copy of the document as originally filed or lodged` MEANS
    IF `the corporation was incorporated or registered under this Act or a corresponding previous written law` AND `the constitution or another document relating to the corporation, filed or lodged with the Registrar, has been lost or destroyed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right arises "If in the case of any corporation incorporated or registered under this Act or any corresponding previous written law the constitution or any other document ... has been lost or destroyed"; the text says nothing of any other case (grant ruling, limit 1)

-- (2): "On such application being made the Registrar may direct notice": "On ... being made" is a "when": JUST FALSE when no application has been made (periods ruling (b); split site (ii), fork line F-H-S1).
-- src:3431 | (2) On such application being made the Registrar may direct notice
-- src:3432 | thereof to be given to such persons and in such manner as the
-- src:3433 | Registrar thinks fit.
@ref s 14(2) (src:3431-3433)
GIVEN `an application under subsection (1) has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(2) the Registrar may direct notice of the application to be given to such persons and in such manner as the Registrar thinks fit` MEANS
    IF `an application under subsection (1) has been made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On such application being made the Registrar may direct notice thereof to be given" (a failed "when": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); split site (ii), fork line F-H-S1)

-- (3): "The Registrar upon being satisfied -- (a) ...; (b) ...; and (c) ... -- may certify ... and direct": "upon being satisfied" is a "when" (split site (ii)).
-- src:3435 | (3) The Registrar upon being satisfied —
-- src:3437 | (a) that the original document has been lost or destroyed;
-- src:3439 | (b) of the date of the filing or lodging thereof with the
-- src:3440 | Registrar; and
-- src:3442 | (c) that a copy of such document produced to the Registrar is a
-- src:3443 | correct copy,
-- src:3445 | may certify upon that copy that the Registrar is so satisfied and direct
-- src:3446 | that that copy be lodged in the manner required by law in respect of
-- src:3447 | the original.
@ref s 14(3) (src:3435-3447)
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the original document has been lost or destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied of the date of the filing or lodging of the original document with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that a copy of the document produced to the Registrar is a correct copy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(3) the Registrar may certify upon the copy that the Registrar is so satisfied and direct that the copy be lodged in the manner required by law in respect of the original` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar is satisfied that the original document has been lost or destroyed` AND `the Registrar is satisfied of the date of the filing or lodging of the original document with the Registrar` AND `the Registrar is satisfied that a copy of the document produced to the Registrar is a correct copy`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar upon being satisfied -- (a) that the original document has been lost or destroyed; (b) of the date of the filing or lodging thereof with the Registrar; and (c) that a copy of such document produced to the Registrar is a correct copy, may certify" (a failed "upon": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); split site (ii), fork line F-H-S1)

