`s 14(4) the copy has for all purposes the same force and effect as the original` MEANS
    IF `the copy has been lodged on a direction under subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon the lodgment, that copy for all purposes has ... the same force and effect as the original" (a failed "upon": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b))

-- src:3449 | (4) Upon the lodgment, that copy for all purposes has, from such
-- src:3450 | date as is mentioned in the certificate as the date of the filing or
-- src:3455 | lodging of the original with the Registrar, the same force and effect as
-- src:3456 | the original.
@ref s 14(4) (src:3449-3456)
GIVEN `the copy has been lodged on a direction under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date mentioned in the certificate as the date of the filing or lodging of the original` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
