    IF `the order is an order of the Court under subsection (5) confirming, varying or rescinding the certificate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the order may be lodged with the Registrar" speaks of the Court's order under this subsection; the text says nothing of any other order

-- src:3461 | lodged with the Registrar and must be registered by the Registrar, but
@ref s 14(5) (src:3461)
GIVEN `the order of the Court under subsection (5) has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(5) the Registrar must register the order` MEANS
    IF `the order of the Court under subsection (5) has been lodged with the Registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the order may be lodged with the Registrar and must be registered by the Registrar" (a duty whose "and" follows the lodging: the provision's own question; marginal reading (a))

-- The saving: "no payments, contracts, dealings, acts and things made, had or done in good faith before the registration of such order and upon the faith of and in reliance upon the certificate are invalidated or affected by such variation or rescission."
-- src:3461 | lodged with the Registrar and must be registered by the Registrar, but
