      `it was made, had or done before the registration of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was made, had or done upon the faith of and in reliance upon the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(5) the payment, contract, dealing, act or thing is invalidated or affected by the variation or rescission` MEANS
    IF `the order of the Court varies or rescinds the certificate` AND `the payment, contract, dealing, act or thing was made, had or done in good faith` AND `it was made, had or done before the registration of the order` AND `it was made, had or done upon the faith of and in reliance upon the certificate`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no payments, contracts, dealings, acts and things made, had or done in good faith before the registration of such order and upon the faith of and in reliance upon the certificate are invalidated or affected by such variation or rescission" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence protects only what meets all of its limbs; the text says nothing of the effect of a variation or rescission on anything else

