§ `Section 15: size, durability and legibility of documents delivered to the Registrar`

-- (1): the Minister's power to prescribe requirements by regulations: machinery (NOTES.md: inert, reason 2).

-- (2): "If under any such provision there is delivered to the Registrar a document ... which in the opinion of the Registrar does not comply ..., the Registrar may serve on any person by whom ... the document was required to be delivered ... a notice": a grant gated by "If" (NOTHING when the gate fails).
-- src:3481 | (2) If under any such provision there is delivered to the Registrar a
-- src:3482 | document (whether an original document or a copy) which in the
-- src:3483 | opinion of the Registrar does not comply with such requirements
-- src:3484 | prescribed under this section as are applicable to it, the Registrar may
-- src:3485 | serve on any person by whom under that provision the document was
-- src:3486 | required to be delivered (or, if there are 2 or more such persons, may
-- src:3487 | serve on any of them) a notice stating the Registrar’s opinion to that
-- src:3488 | effect and indicating the requirements so prescribed with which in the
-- src:3489 | Registrar’s opinion the document does not comply.
@ref s 15(2) (src:3481-3489)
GIVEN `a document, whether an original document or a copy, has been delivered to the Registrar under a provision of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the Registrar the document does not comply with the requirements prescribed under section 15 that apply to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person by whom under that provision the document was required to be delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(2) the Registrar may serve on the person a notice stating the Registrar's opinion and the requirements with which the document does not comply` MEANS
    IF `a document, whether an original document or a copy, has been delivered to the Registrar under a provision of this Act` AND `in the opinion of the Registrar the document does not comply with the requirements prescribed under section 15 that apply to it` AND `the person is a person by whom under that provision the document was required to be delivered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Registrar "may serve on any person by whom under that provision the document was required to be delivered" a notice where "in the opinion of the Registrar" the document does not comply; the text says nothing of any other case (grant ruling, limit 1)

-- src:3491 | (3) Where the Registrar serves a notice under subsection (2) with
-- src:3492 | respect to a document delivered under any such provision, then, for
-- src:3493 | the purposes of any written law which enables a penalty to be
-- src:3494 | imposed in respect of any omission to deliver to the Registrar a
-- src:3495 | document required to be delivered under that provision (and, in
-- src:3500 | particular, for the purposes of any such law whereby such a penalty
-- src:3501 | may be imposed by reference to each day during which the omission
-- src:3502 | continues) —
@ref s 15(3) (src:3491-3502)
GIVEN `the Registrar has served a notice under subsection (2) with respect to the document delivered under the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(3)(a) the duty to deliver the document is treated as not having been discharged by the delivery of that document` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has served a notice under subsection (2) with respect to the document delivered under the provision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Registrar serves a notice under subsection (2) with respect to a document delivered under any such provision, then, for the purposes of any written law which enables a penalty to be imposed ... (a) any duty imposed by that provision to deliver such a document to the Registrar is to be treated as not having been discharged by the delivery of that document" (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); the answer means only that this deeming does not apply)

-- (4): "The period referred to in subsection (3)(b) is the period beginning on the day on which the document was delivered to the Registrar as mentioned in subsection (2) and ending on the 14th day after the date of service of the notice".
-- A definition ("is the period"): the day is in it or the text says no.
