GIVEN `the day on which the document was delivered to the Registrar` IS A DATE
      `the date of service of the notice under subsection (2)` IS A DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(4) the day falls within the period mentioned in subsection (3)(b)` MEANS
    `the day` AT LEAST `the day on which the document was delivered to the Registrar`
    AND `the day` AT MOST `s 15(4) the last day of the period mentioned in subsection (3)(b)` `the day on which the document was delivered to the Registrar` `the date of service of the notice under subsection (2)`

-- src:3504 | (a) any duty imposed by that provision to deliver such a
-- src:3505 | document to the Registrar is to be treated as not having
-- src:3506 | been discharged by the delivery of that document; but
-- src:3508 | (b) no account is to be taken of any days falling within the
-- src:3509 | period mentioned in subsection (4).
@ref s 15(3) (src:3504-3509)
GIVEN `the Registrar has served a notice under subsection (2) with respect to the document delivered under the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the document was delivered to the Registrar` IS A DATE
      `the date of service of the notice under subsection (2)` IS A DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(3)(b) no account is taken of the day in applying a penalty imposed by reference to each day during which the omission continues` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has served a notice under subsection (2) with respect to the document delivered under the provision` AND `s 15(4) the day falls within the period mentioned in subsection (3)(b)` `the day on which the document was delivered to the Registrar` `the date of service of the notice under subsection (2)` `the day`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no account is to be taken of any days falling within the period mentioned in subsection (4)" (a failed "where", or a day outside the period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (a) and (b); the answer means only that this exclusion does not apply to the day)

-- (5): "any reference to delivering a document is to be construed as including a reference to sending, forwarding, producing or (in the case of a notice) giving it": an "includes" (the term stays open).
DECLARE `s 15(5) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 15(5) delivering the document`
    `s 15(5) sending the document`
    `s 15(5) forwarding the document`
    `s 15(5) producing the document`
    `s 15(5) giving the document`
    `s 15(5) some other act`

-- src:3517 | (5) In this section, any reference to delivering a document is to be
-- src:3518 | construed as including a reference to sending, forwarding, producing
-- src:3519 | or (in the case of a notice) giving it.
@ref s 15(5) (src:3517-3519)
GIVEN act IS A `s 15(5) act`
      `the document is a notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(5) the act is a delivery of the document` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 15(5) delivering the document` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 15(5) sending the document` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 15(5) forwarding the document` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 15(5) producing the document` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 15(5) giving the document` THEN (IF `the document is a notice` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "or (in the case of a notice) giving it"; the text says nothing of giving a document that is not a notice
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "is to be construed as including a reference to sending, forwarding, producing or ... giving it" leaves the term open

§ `Regulative rule of s 14(5): no time limit and no consequence the text states, so no breach path`

DECLARE `s 14 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 14(5) register the order of the Court lodged with the Registrar`

-- src:3458 | (5) The Court may, by order upon application by any person
-- src:3459 | aggrieved and after notice to any other person whom the Court
-- src:3460 | directs, confirm, vary or rescind the certificate and the order may be
-- src:3461 | lodged with the Registrar and must be registered by the Registrar, but
@ref s 14(5) (src:3458-3461)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 14 act`
`s 14(5) rule: the Registrar's duty to register the order` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 14(5) register the order of the Court lodged with the Registrar`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 14(5) gives this duty no deadline in days (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
